//@version=6
// =============================================================================================
// NQ — BOS/CHoCH, the two-leg book that produced the best positive results
//
// RUN IT TWICE, on two charts, same symbol:
//     chart 1 — 30 minutes, preset "30m core"   (range filter ON, 1.0 x ATR)
//     chart 2 — 60 minutes, preset "60m core"   (range filter OFF)
// The two legs correlate 0.28. Neither is the answer on its own; the pair is.
//
// v3 FIXES THE SESSION GATE (see grpT). v2 fixed the stop anchor: the stop was placed at `close - 2*ATR` measured on the SIGNAL bar,
// but the fill happens at the NEXT bar's open. Every stop sat at the wrong distance. It is now
// anchored to strategy.position_avg_price, which is the actual fill.
// =============================================================================================

// !! TIMEFRAME MATTERS MORE THAN ANY SETTING. Use 30m or 60m. On 5m this rule LOSES: my own
// !! engine gives PF 0.96-0.99 there, and coin-flip entries with the same stop beat it 65% of the
// !! time. On 1m and 2m it is significantly negative (t = -2.45, -2.68). A losing 5-minute
// !! backtest is not a bug, it is the documented result.

// v6 FIXES THE ENTRY GATE, which was the only real logic divergence from the tested engine.
// With it corrected this script reproduces the reference engine EXACTLY on 30m over
// Dec-2022..Dec-2025: 147 trades, $71,483, PF 1.54, 40.1% win. The previous session-string entry
// window admitted the session's FIRST bar, which the engine excludes; that one extra bar per day
// was worth 35 extra trades and -$8,318. The `strategy.position_size` one-bar lag and the
// statement ordering, which earlier versions of this comment blamed, contribute nothing.
//
// !! READING A MISMATCHED RESULT. The win rate is a fingerprint of the STOP MULTIPLE, nothing
// !! else. Measured on my engine over Dec-2022..Dec-2025, 30m, both under this script's exact
// !! control flow and under the reference engine:
// !!        stop 2.0 x ATR  ->  win 39-40%   (CHoCH exits 62-75% of closes)   <- the tested spec
// !!        stop 1.0 x ATR  ->  win 27-29%   (CHoCH exits 37-41% of closes)
// !!        stop 0.5 x ATR  ->  win 16-17%
// !! So a backtest printing ~27% win rate is running a 1 x ATR stop, whatever the input box says
// !! — TradingView caches inputs per chart and a stale value survives a script update. That is
// !! what "LOCK the tested spec" below is for. Trade COUNT is the fingerprint of nBos: ~150-190
// !! at nBos=2, ~290-400 at nBos=1, same window. Check both against the diagnostic label.

strategy("NQ BOS/CHoCH book", overlay = true, initial_capital = 100000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_order,
     commission_value = input.float(2.00, "Commission $ per order  (NQ 2.00 / MNQ 0.50)",
         group = "Costs",
         tooltip = "READ THIS IF YOUR RESULT IS NEGATIVE. 2.00 is right for NQ (E-mini, $20/pt). " +
                   "The sizing note at the bottom of this script tells you to trade MNQ (Micro, " +
                   "$2/pt) because a 2xATR stop on NQ risks ~$2,000 a contract — but MNQ is 10x " +
                   "smaller and this fee is NOT, so leaving it at 2.00 on MNQ charges ~10x too " +
                   "much. Measured: identical trades score 0.5% of gross profit in commission on " +
                   "NQ and 5.2% on MNQ at 2.00/order, which is enough to flatten the book. Set " +
                   "0.50 on MNQ. The diagnostic label warns you if this looks wrong."),
     slippage = 2, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false,
     process_orders_on_close = false)

// ── preset ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
preset = input.string("30m core", "Preset", options = ["30m core", "60m core", "custom"],
     tooltip = "30m core: range filter 1.0 ATR.  60m core: range filter off. " +
               "Run BOTH on separate charts — that is the tested book.")

grpS = "Structure"
swingK  = input.int(3, "Swing confirmation bars (k)", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grpS,
     tooltip = "A pivot needs k bars either side, so it is invisible until k bars later. " +
               "k had a DIFFERENT best value at every timeframe tested — it is the fragile axis. " +
               "Left at the neutral 3 deliberately.")
nBosIn  = input.int(2, "Enter on the Nth BOS", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = grpS)
lockSpec= input.bool(true, "LOCK the tested spec (ignore cached chart settings)", group = grpS,
     tooltip = "TradingView remembers input values PER CHART. If this script was added before a " +
               "revision, your saved values persist and silently override the defaults. With this " +
               "on, the entry count and stop multiple are forced to the tested values.")
nBos    = lockSpec ? 2 : nBosIn

grpF = "Filters"
useEma  = input.bool(true, "Require price on the trend side of the EMA", group = grpF)
emaLen  = input.int(200, "EMA length", minval = 10, group = grpF)
mdIn    = input.float(1.0, "Refuse entries within N x ATR of the EMA", minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = grpF)

grpR = "Risk"
atrLen  = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 2, group = grpR)
atrMultIn = input.float(2.0, "Stop = N x ATR", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = grpR)
atrMult   = lockSpec ? 2.0 : atrMultIn
useChoch= input.bool(true, "Exit on the opposite BOS (CHoCH)", group = grpR)

grpV = "Volatility-targeted sizing"
useVTIn = input.bool(false, "Size inversely to recent volatility", group = grpV,
     tooltip = "OFF by default because the headline result this script is meant to reproduce " +
               "($71,483 / PF 1.54 / 40.1% win, 147 trades, 30m) was measured at a FIXED 1 " +
               "contract. Turning this on is a separate, separately-validated overlay: max " +
               "drawdown fell from 36.3% to 10.5% while Sharpe ROSE from 1.31 to 1.60. It changes " +
               "size only, never direction — so trade count and win rate are unaffected, but the " +
               "P&L will no longer match the reference figures.")
useVT   = lockSpec ? false : useVTIn
vtLook  = input.int(60, "Volatility lookback (bars)", minval = 10, group = grpV)
vtCap   = input.float(2.0, "Maximum size multiplier", minval = 1.0, step = 0.5, group = grpV)
baseQty = input.float(1.0, "Base contracts", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpV)

grpT = "Session (exchange time)"
// THE ENTRY GATE. This is the one place a previous version diverged from the tested engine, and
// it was worth 35 extra trades and -$8,318 on 30m. The engine admits an entry only when ALL THREE
// hold, and the third is the one that was missing:
//     1. the signal bar is in session
//     2. the NEXT bar is also in session   -- the fill is at the next open, and an entry that
//        fills at 16:00 is filling after the cash close in thin liquidity
//     3. the signal bar is NOT the session's first bar
// Expressed as clock arithmetic on the bar's OPEN time in exchange timezone, which is exact and
// involves no look-ahead: the calendar is known in advance, the prices are not. At 30m this
// admits 10:00 through 15:00. Do not replace it with an input.session() window — a session string
// cannot express "the next bar is also inside", which is condition 2.
sessStart = input.int(570, "Session start (minutes after midnight, exchange time)", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "570 = 09:30. Change only to test a different session.")
sessEnd   = input.int(960, "Session end (minutes after midnight, exchange time)", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "960 = 16:00.")
showSess = input.bool(true, "Tint the entry window", group = grpT)

showDiag = input.bool(false, "Show diagnostics (run counter, entries, settings in force)",
     group = "Diagnostics",
     tooltip = "Turn this on to confirm the gates are actually gating. The label on the last bar " +
               "reports the values IN FORCE, which is the only way to catch a cached input.")

minDist = preset == "30m core" ? 1.0 : preset == "60m core" ? 0.0 : mdIn

// ── indicators ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
emaV = ta.ema(close, emaLen)
atrV = ta.atr(atrLen)

// Confirmed fractal pivots. ta.pivothigh(k,k) returns the pivot k bars back, so reading it on the
// current bar is causal: the value does not exist until the right-hand bars have printed.
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, swingK, swingK)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  swingK, swingK)
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if not na(ph)
    lastPH := ph
if not na(pl)
    lastPL := pl

// ── structure ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var float brokeHi = na
var float brokeLo = na
var int   bias    = 0
var int   runLen  = 0

bosUp = not na(lastPH) and close > lastPH and (na(brokeHi) or lastPH != brokeHi)
bosDn = not na(lastPL) and close < lastPL and (na(brokeLo) or lastPL != brokeLo)
if bosUp
    brokeHi := lastPH
if bosDn
    brokeLo := lastPL
// The counter must be tested against the OLD bias and only then reassigned. Writing
// `bias := 1` first makes the following test trivially true and the run counter never resets on a
// structure flip -- which silently turns "enter on the second BOS" into "enter on every BOS".
if bosUp
    if bias == 1
        runLen := runLen + 1
    else
        bias   := 1
        runLen := 1
if bosDn
    if bias == -1
        runLen := runLen + 1
    else
        bias   := -1
        runLen := 1

// ── session gate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
flatEOD  = input.bool(false, "Flatten at the session close (intraday-only variant)", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "OFF = the tested spec: a position is held until its stop or a CHoCH, which on 30m " +
               "means a 12.5h median hold and 35% of trades crossing the close. ON = forced flat " +
               "daily. Measured over Dec-2022..Dec-2025 on 30m: holding gives $63,165 / PF 1.38 / " +
               "39.0% win, flattening gives $47,997 / PF 1.29 / 44.4% win. BUT that is the full " +
               "sample. Split on the same research/locked-holdout boundary used elsewhere in this " +
               "work, the ranking FLIPS: on research, flattening wins (Sharpe 1.96 vs 1.68); on the " +
               "LOCKED third, holding wins decisively ($32,642 / Sharpe 1.87 vs $15,182 / 0.95). " +
               "Flattening is in-sample-attractive and out-of-sample-inferior, so turn it on for " +
               "RISK reasons only — no overnight gap exposure, day-trade margin, a prop-firm " +
               "flat-by-close rule — and expect it to COST roughly half the P&L and half the " +
               "Sharpe, not the 24% the full sample suggests. It is not the tested spec, and it is " +
               "not a free improvement. (Locked block is 69-76 trades: directional, not decisive.)")
tfMin    = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) / 60
barMin   = hour * 60 + minute                          // bar OPEN, exchange timezone
inSess   = barMin >= sessStart and barMin < sessEnd
nextIn   = barMin + tfMin >= sessStart and barMin + tfMin < sessEnd
newSess  = inSess and not inSess[1]
canEnter = inSess and nextIn and not newSess

// ── filters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
farEnough = minDist <= 0 or (not na(emaV) and not na(atrV) and math.abs(close - emaV) >= minDist * atrV)
okLong  = (not useEma or close > emaV) and farEnough
okShort = (not useEma or close < emaV) and farEnough
ready   = not na(atrV) and atrV > 0 and not na(emaV)

longSig  = bosUp and runLen >= nBos and okLong  and canEnter and ready
shortSig = bosDn and runLen >= nBos and okShort and canEnter and ready

// ── volatility-targeted size: bigger when quiet, smaller when wild. Causal. ──────────────────
avgAtr = ta.sma(atrV, vtLook)
vtMult = useVT and not na(avgAtr) and atrV > 0 ? math.min(avgAtr / atrV, vtCap) : 1.0
qty    = math.max(math.round(baseQty * vtMult), 1)

// ── orders ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The stop is anchored to the ACTUAL fill (strategy.position_avg_price), not to the signal bar's
// close. The ATR used is the one that was current when the signal fired.
var float atrAtSignal = na
var float stopLevel   = na

if (longSig or shortSig) and strategy.position_size == 0
    atrAtSignal := atrV

if longSig and strategy.position_size == 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty = qty)
if shortSig and strategy.position_size == 0
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty = qty)

if strategy.position_size > 0 and na(stopLevel)
    stopLevel := strategy.position_avg_price - atrMult * atrAtSignal
if strategy.position_size < 0 and na(stopLevel)
    stopLevel := strategy.position_avg_price + atrMult * atrAtSignal
if strategy.position_size == 0
    stopLevel := na

if strategy.position_size > 0 and not na(stopLevel)
    strategy.exit("Lx", "L", stop = stopLevel)
if strategy.position_size < 0 and not na(stopLevel)
    strategy.exit("Sx", "S", stop = stopLevel)

// Track why positions close, so a win-rate mismatch can be attributed rather than guessed at.
var int nCloses = 0
var int nChoch = 0
wasIn = strategy.position_size[1] != 0
if wasIn and strategy.position_size == 0
    nCloses += 1

if flatEOD and strategy.position_size != 0 and not inSess
    strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD flat")

if useChoch
    if strategy.position_size > 0 and bosDn
        strategy.close("L", comment = "CHoCH")
        nChoch += 1
    if strategy.position_size < 0 and bosUp
        strategy.close("S", comment = "CHoCH")
        nChoch += 1

if showDiag and barstate.islast
    var label lbl = na
    label.delete(lbl)
    lbl := label.new(bar_index, high, "symbol: " + syminfo.ticker + "  tf: " + timeframe.period +
         "\n$ per point: " + str.tostring(syminfo.pointvalue) + "   (NQ = 20, MNQ = 2)" +
         "\nposition closes: " + str.tostring(nCloses) +
         "\nCHoCH signals: " + str.tostring(nChoch) +
         "\nstop-outs (closes - CHoCH): " + str.tostring(nCloses - nChoch) +
         "\nnBos in force: " + str.tostring(nBos) +
         "\nvol-targeted sizing: " + (useVT ? "ON (P&L will not match reference)" : "off") +
         "\nentry window: " + str.tostring(math.round(sessStart + tfMin)) + "-" + str.tostring(math.round(sessEnd - tfMin)) +
         " min (exchange)" +
         "\nstop mult: " + str.tostring(atrMult) +
         "\nrange filter: " + str.tostring(minDist) +
         (syminfo.pointvalue < 10 and strategy.commission.value >= 1.5 ?
             "\n\n*** COST MISMATCH: this looks like a Micro contract ($" +
             str.tostring(syminfo.pointvalue) + "/pt) charged an E-mini fee. Set commission to " +
             "0.50/order or the fee alone will sink the result. ***" : ""),
         style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.black, 20), textcolor = color.white)

// ── plots ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plot(emaV, "EMA 200", color.new(color.orange, 0), 2)
bU = plot(minDist > 0 ? emaV + minDist * atrV : na, "no-trade band", color.new(color.gray, 70))
bL = plot(minDist > 0 ? emaV - minDist * atrV : na, "no-trade band", color.new(color.gray, 70))
fill(bU, bL, color.new(color.gray, 92), title = "range — no entries here")
plot(stopLevel, "stop", color.new(color.red, 0), 1, plot.style_linebr)
// Structure markers only inside the session -- v2 plotted them on all 24 hours, which made an
// RTH-only strategy look like it was signalling overnight.
// DIAGNOSTICS — turn these on to see whether the gates are actually gating.
plotchar(showDiag ? runLen : na, "BOS run counter", "", location.top, color.new(color.yellow, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotchar(showDiag ? (longSig or shortSig ? 1 : na) : na, "entry fired", "E", location.bottom, color.new(color.lime, 0), size = size.tiny)

plotshape(bosUp and inSess, "BOS up",   shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.new(color.teal, 0),   size = size.tiny)
plotshape(bosDn and inSess, "BOS down", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.maroon, 0), size = size.tiny)
bgcolor(showSess and canEnter ? color.new(color.blue, 94) : na, title = "entry window")

// =============================================================================================
// THE NUMBERS THESE RULES PRODUCED — docs/ib/STUDY_BOS_CHOCH.md, STUDY_LOWER_DD.md
// NQ, Dec 2022 – Dec 2025, $19–24 per round turn, 1 contract, no volatility sizing:
//
//   30m leg (filter 1.0)   147 trades   +$71,483   PF 1.54   Sharpe 1.00   maxDD 15.6%   t 1.88
//   60m leg (filter 0)      43 trades   +$63,233   PF 2.37   Sharpe 1.08   maxDD 13.1%
//   BOTH, inverse-vol weighted, volatility-targeted:
//                                       +$149,507  Sharpe 1.60   maxDD 10.5%   Calmar 3.36
//
//   LOCKED final third (268 sessions, never used to choose anything):
//     30m +$47,072 Sharpe 1.39   |   60m +$28,065 Sharpe 1.07
//     both, vol-targeted:  +$72,075   Sharpe 2.02   maxDD 11.8%   Calmar 5.62
//
// WHAT FAILS, so you do not rediscover it:
//   • 1m and 2m are SIGNIFICANTLY NEGATIVE (t = −2.45, −2.68). This does not scalp.
//   • At 5m, coin-flip entries with the same risk management beat it 65% of the time.
//   • Adding a 15m leg RAISED book drawdown to 37% for a Calmar of 0.26. Two legs, not three.
//   • An equity-curve brake (cut size after an 8% drawdown) made everything worse — it de-risks
//     into the loss and is too small for the recovery.
//   • PBO is 0.571 and t = 1.88 against a ~2.7 multiple-testing hurdle. The strategy is
//     profitable and out-of-sample positive; it is NOT a statistically established edge.
//   • There is NO ES DATA behind any of this. One instrument, one bull market.
//
// SIZE: a 2×ATR stop on 30m NQ risks ~$2,000 per contract. At $100–$300 risk per trade every
// signal rounds to zero contracts. Use MNQ, where the same stop is ~$200 — AND THEN SET THE
// COMMISSION INPUT TO 0.50. Every dollar figure quoted above is NQ at $20/pt; on MNQ divide them
// by 10. The two instructions have to be followed together: MNQ sizing with an NQ fee charges ten
// times the real cost and turns this book negative on its own.
//
// Research tooling for education and analysis. Not financial advice.
// =============================================================================================
